- op: discuss  # 55b9
  at: '2026-03-18T17:29:05Z'  # 55b9
  by: agent  # 55b9
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 55b9
  clock: 2  # 55b9
  nonce: 55b9  # 55b9
  message: "Profiling on killbill (1688 Java files, 30s total):\n- iter_tree: 9.6s (33%) — 11M function calls for tree traversal\n- _find_node_at_line: 4.3s (15%) — called 37K times, O(n) per call\n- _extract_edges: 6.9s (23%)\n- _extract_symbols: 4.0s (14%)\n- _extract_imports: 2.7s (9%)\n\nBiggest optimization opportunities:\n1. _find_node_at_line is O(n*m) — building a line→node index would reduce to O(m)\n2. iter_tree could be optimized by avoiding Python function call overhead (11M calls)\n3. For Flink (14K files), these scale roughly 8x → ~4 min estimated. The observed 100+ min suggests super-linear scaling in one of these, likely name resolution (259K lookups in killbill → ~2M+ for Flink)."  # 55b9
